  "interpretation": [
    "Absolute acceleration lengths apply the C13 reference density and80percent fill to every listed speed as a common material diagnostic; actual A/B1/B2 source material densities require their own design.",
    "Orbital support guide EM20/cryo hardware is unrelated to the fuel grain accelerator and is not scaled.",
    "At fixed surface field and accelerating gradient,2cm doubles acceleration length and required integrated voltage while halving aggregate current. Larger grains also change focusing strength at fixed lens fields and increase internal thermal equilibration time.",
    "Source mass is currently an aggregate100W/kg peak allocation plus storage/conditioning; the fraction tied to length is not engineered. Thus20.8mW/kg cannot be silently retained, or the whole source mass automatically doubled.",
    "Long protected radial fuel corridors are a separate unfinished geometry; their area/cooling cannot be credited from the orbital support guide.",
    "The counted tube skin is a geometric scale only. Conductors, optics, insulation, field control, supports, shielding, manufacturing and irradiation repair remain outside it."
  ],
